         report_at_maximum_capacity -> llvm::SmallVectorBase<unsigned int>::grow_pod, inside
         IRGen (IRGenSILFunction::visitFullApplySite -> SyncCallEmission::setArgs). 0 source
         errors in any run. The crashing batch varied across runs (AppearanceSettings.* /
         AuditPanel.* / Auth* ; the alphabetic App* batch) — the signature of an allocation
         failure under memory pressure, not a code error.
     * Confirmed cross-worker / shared-host contention: this host runs multiple parallel agent
         slots building the SAME TeslaSync app concurrently. During my builds, observed slot-16
         (p4 0055 AITripPlannerLLMAgent) and slot-18 xcodebuild processes running; free RAM
         swung 0.7-25 GB as slots spiked. Sibling slot-16's own log records the identical issue
         verbatim: "even -jobs 1 was OOM-killed by a SYSTEM-WIDE spike (other slots)".
     * Reproduced on BASELINE without my files: removing all 12 AINLDashboardComposer.* files,
         regenerating, and rebuilding still crashed swift-frontend (1 crash, 0 source errors) on
         a pre-existing batch -> the crash is independent of this surface.
   Mitigations attempted (all advanced the build further; each eventually met another OOM
   swift-frontend crash, never a surface error): freeing RAM, killing my own orphaned builds,
   -jobs 1/2/4/6/8/10 (batch re-partitioning), incremental cache accumulation, isolated
   -derivedDataPath. The surface compiled clean in every attempt.

